The client entrypoint should go under **`StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts`**. Right now it won't run.

In `default.project.json`, `src/client` is mapped to `ReplicatedStorage.Client`. Rojo turns a folder containing `init.client.luau` into a LocalScript, and LocalScripts only run when they sit under `StarterPlayerScripts`, `StarterCharacterScripts`, `StarterGui`, or `StarterPack`. A LocalScript in `ReplicatedStorage` is inert, so `print("client")` never fires. The server side is fine: `ServerScriptService.Server` is a regular Script and will run.

The fix is to change the mapping:

```json
"StarterPlayer": {
  "StarterPlayerScripts": { "Client": { "$path": "src/client" } }
},
```

in place of the current `"Client": { "$path": "src/client" }` entry under `ReplicatedStorage`. Keep `Shared` in `ReplicatedStorage`, since both server and client need it.

I haven't changed anything. Do you want me to make this edit to `default.project.json`?

